    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (81.66) anchoring the lineup, carrying an elite 0.474 xwOBA into a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a. He is joined by **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Trea Turner** (75.43), both of whom capitalize on plus-matchups against right-handed pitching. **Yelich** specifically benefits from an 18% boost driven by the platoon advantage and favorable wind conditions, while **Turner** remains our primary engine for stolen bases, maintaining a high floor despite facing Phillips. **Kyle Schwarber** (71.62) rounds out our top-tier plays; despite a marginal park factor, his volume in the #2 hole and the matchup against Phillips\u2019 4.84 xERA position him for a productive day in the HR and RBI categories.\n\nThe optimization process was most difficult regarding the utility and middle infield spots. **Josh Smith** (47.17) served as the primary internal challenger to **Chase Meidroth** (48.47) and **Caleb Durbin** (51.62). While **Smith** possesses strong platoon dynamics against righties, his spot at the bottom of the order (-6%) ultimately relegated him to the bench in favor of the higher-volume spots occupied by **Durbin** and **Meidroth**. We are monitoring the status of **Dillon Dingler** (47.84) closely; while his base projection is solid, the 15% penalty for the platoon disadvantage against Bradish keeps his efficiency score in the lower quartile of our starters. With no game scheduled for **Junior Caminero** or **Carson Benge**, the roster remains locked, though we are wary of the 10% penalty **Caleb Durbin** faces due to the specialized skill set of Perkins, which serves as the primary risk factor for his otherwise strong projection.",
